---
layout: page
title: Profile
permalink: /profile.html
canonical_url: https://huwdiprose.co.uk/profile
description: WebID profile for Huw Diprose, also available as Turtle and JSON-LD.
rdf_alternates:
  - type: text/turtle
    href: /profile.ttl
  - type: application/ld+json
    href: /profile.jsonld
---
<% webid = site.data.webid %>
<p>
  This is the <a href="https://www.w3.org/2005/Incubator/webid/spec/identity/">WebID</a>
  profile document for <%= webid.name %>. Linked-data clients requesting
  <code>text/turtle</code> or <code>application/ld+json</code> from this
  address get the same statements as RDF. They are also available directly
  as <a href="/profile.ttl">Turtle</a> and <a href="/profile.jsonld">JSON-LD</a>.
</p>

<dl class="webid-profile">
  <dt>WebID</dt>
  <dd><code class="webid-person"><%= webid.person %></code></dd>

  <dt>Name</dt>
  <dd class="webid-name"><%= webid.name %></dd>

  <dt>Avatar</dt>
  <dd><img class="webid-image" src="<%= webid.image %>" alt="<%= webid.name %>" width="96" height="96"></dd>

  <dt>Homepage</dt>
  <dd><a class="webid-homepage" href="<%= webid.homepage %>"><%= webid.homepage %></a></dd>

  <dt>Solid login issuer</dt>
  <dd><code class="webid-oidc-issuer"><%= webid.oidc_issuer %></code></dd>

  <dt>Solid Pod</dt>
  <dd><code class="webid-storage"><%= webid.storage %></code></dd>

  <dt>Accounts</dt>
  <dd>
    <ul>
      <% webid.accounts.each do |account| %>
      <li><a class="webid-account" href="<%= account.url %>"><%= account.label %></a></li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
  </dd>
</dl>
